{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423846","formula":"C₅₆H₁₀₈O₃₀","hill":"C56H108O30","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":56.0,"H":108.0,"O":30.0},"names":{"en":"Hypromellose","ru":"Метилоксипропилцеллюлоза"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hypromellose (INN), short for hydroxypropyl methylcellulose or hydroxypropylmethylcellulose (HPMC), is a semisynthetic, inert, viscoelastic polymer used in eye drops, as well as an excipient and controlled-delivery component in oral medicaments, found in a variety of commercial products. As a food additive, hypromellose is an emulsifier, thickening and suspending agent, and an alternative to animal gelatin. Its Codex Alimentarius code (E number) is E464.","ru":"Оксипропилметилцеллюлоза, или гидроксипропилметилцеллюлоза (ГПМЦ) — смешанный эфир на основе метилцеллюлозы, содержащий в элементарном звене макромолекулы целлюлозы наряду с метоксильными гидроксипропильные группы. В нормальных условиях — твёрдое вещество (порошок)."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":57503849,"mass":1261.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(COC[C@@H]1[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H](O1)O[C@@H]2[C@H](O[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]2OCC(C)O)OCC(C)O)OCC(C)O)COCC(C)O)OCC(C)O)OCC(C)O)OCC(C)O)O.COC[C@@H]1[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]([C@@H](O1)O[C@@H]2[C@H](O[C@H]([C@@H]([C@H]2OC)OC)OC)COC)OC)OC)OC","inchikey":"PUSNGFYSTWMJSK-GSZQVNRLSA-N","iupac":"(2R,3R,4S,5R,6R)-2,3,4-trimethoxy-6-(methoxymethyl)-5-[(2S,3R,4S,5R,6R)-3,4,5-trimethoxy-6-(methoxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyoxane;1-[[(2R,3R,4S,5R,6S)-3,4,5-tris(2-hydroxypropoxy)-6-[(2R,3R,4S,5R,6R)-4,5,6-tris(2-hydroxypropoxy)-2-(2-hydroxypropoxymethyl)oxan-3-yl]oxyoxan-2-yl]methoxy]propan-2-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"57503849","atoms":194,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.096,"y":1.138,"z":4.145,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.656,"y":1.048,